.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt NETD 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm netd
.Nd RavenBSD net: socket server over loopback
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /sbin/netd
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs the native socket core with IPv4 loopback configured
.Pq Li 127.0.0.1/8 ,
registers the
.Dq net:
scheme and serves one file per socket plus the
.Pa net:
control file.
.Pp
The first milestone has one interface,
.Dq lo ;
the virtio-net frame ring is the B12b seam and is not wired in this binary.
IPv6 is not configured.
.Pp
Scheme paths are:
.Bl -tag -width "net:tcp/<ipv4>:<port>" -compact
.It Pa net:
interface control channel
.It Pa net:tcp/ Ns Ar ipv4 : Ns Ar port
TCP socket; the path endpoint is the listener endpoint for
.Dv LISTEN
and the remote endpoint for
.Dv CONNECT
.It Pa net:udp/ Ns Ar ipv4 : Ns Ar port
UDP socket
.El
.Pp
After
.Dv OPEN ,
the client uses the S11
.Dv CALL
operation with a
.Xr raven-proto-net 3
.Dv SocketRequest
message.  The supported calls are
.Dv BIND ,
.Dv LISTEN ,
.Dv ACCEPT ,
.Dv CONNECT ,
.Dv SHUTDOWN ,
.Dv GETSOCKNAME ,
.Dv GETPEERNAME ,
.Dv SETSOCKOPT ,
.Dv GETSOCKOPT
and
.Dv EVENT .
A successful
.Dv ACCEPT
returns a numeric socket id; the client opens
.Pa net:accept/<id>
to materialise the SchemeFile handle for that connection.  This is the
ABI-v1 substitute for an S25 attachment: there is no server-side file-create
primitive, so the accepted descriptor is opened explicitly.  B12b may replace
it with the standard attachment path when the protocol grows one.
.Pp
.Dv READ
and
.Dv WRITE
move stream bytes for TCP.  A typed
.Dv SocketRequest::Read
returns a
.Dv Response::Read
header followed by the datagram payload and the source endpoint for UDP;
.Dv SocketRequest::Write
carries an optional destination endpoint.  A raw UDP write is accepted only
after
.Dv CONNECT
sets a peer.
.Pp
.Dv EVENT
returns an S25
.Dv UserEvent
attachment in the
.Dv CALL
reply.  The client registers that handle in an S26 event queue and waits for
readable, writable, accepted or closed transitions rather than retrying with
sleeps.  The server itself blocks in
.Dv EVQ_WAIT
on the scheme-server handle and uses the stack's next-timer delay as the
timeout, so stack timers still run without a heartbeat thread.
.Pp
.Dv TCP_NODELAY
is applied to the native TCP socket.
.Dv SO_REUSEADDR ,
.Dv SO_RCVBUF
and
.Dv SO_SNDBUF
are retained per socket and reported back by
.Dv GETSOCKOPT ;
the native stack in this revision has no per-socket bind or buffer knob, so
those values do not alter stack behaviour yet.
.Pp
The control file accepts
.Dv IfaceRequest
messages.  In this milestone
.Dv LIST
returns one
.Dq lo
record and
.Dv ARP_LIST
returns an empty table;
.Dv SET_ADDRESS
and
.Dv SET_STATE
update the loopback record, while route operations return
.Er EOPNOTSUPP .
.Pp
The server polls the native stack after each request and after each event
wakeup; clients sleep only when they do not ask for a readiness event.
The qtest uses a client/server pair inside one probe process, waits on the
.Dv EVENT
doorbells, checks TCP and UDP bytes, the accept path, local/peer endpoints,
socket options and orderly close, lists
.Dq lo ,
restarts
.Nm
once through
.Xr svcctl 1 ,
and runs the same probe again to show that the socket table was released.
There is no host networking and no virtio-net device in this test.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d/netd.toml -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/netd.toml
service manifest
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr svcctl 1 ,
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr vfsd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
server first appeared in RavenBSD 0.1.
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1; `raven-proto-net` protocol version 1.
